SPURS job chains: no synthetic completion events; ShutdownJobChain really stops the walker. Toro's own patch (7xxx).
What: (1) jc_execute/jc_thread no longer push (data1 = chain EA, data2 = job counter) to every queue attached with
cellSpursAttachLv2EventQueue after each JOB, at END and at walker exit. On hardware a job chain posts nothing there:
Attach connects the queue to the SPURS SPU thread group, so its only events are those SPU code sends itself with
sys_spu_thread_send_event, which the lv2 user-event path already routes for job contexts (spurs_port_queue).
Toro's sound jobs ("soc-job") send (port 16, slot index, query answer) themselves; the game writes the attached port
into the job descriptor (@0x1F28F8) and reads data2 low word as slot index, data3 as answer (@0x1F294C..0x1F2A18).
The synthetic event duplicated them with data2 = a counter over the whole walk (412 seen), which made the pump
@0x1F27E0 index past its ~127-slot table, and it filled the queue so the job's own send got EBUSY (0x8001000A).
Old behaviour kept as opt-in fallback for titles whose job images are not lifted: SPURS_JC_SYNTH_EVENTS=1.
(2) ShutdownJobChain requested nothing: it cleared `running` while the walker stayed parked at its GUARD, so the
game's Shutdown+Join (@0x1F26A8/0x1F26B4) returned at once and the following Create+Run started a second walker on
the same chain and guard (15 RunJobChain on one chain in a 60 s run). Now Shutdown sets a per-chain stop flag the
walker polls at each command and inside the guard wait; `running` is cleared by the walker thread on exit, so Join
waits for the real stop (hardware: cellSpursShutdownWorkload / WaitForWorkloadShutdown, [src:RPCS3-CELLSPURS]).
A Run after an un-joined Shutdown waits for the old walker to leave.
Test: build tlp.exe; in a run, "[cellSpurs] job chain completion events: none" once, no "job N done -> event
queue" lines, "[spu-evt] ... port 16 -> queue 4" with rc=0x0 (no 0x8001000A), "chain 0x4023E900: shut down
after N job(s)" before each re-Run, and no unresolved calls / NULL reads from func_001F27E0 (lr 0x1F29D4).
Upstream candidate (behaviour change for titles that relied on the synthetic event: needs their jobs lifted or the
env fallback).

